 ### Veterinarian directory
 
-<a id="req-vet-001"></a>
+<a id="req-vet-001"></a><a id="req-vet-003"></a><a id="req-vet-004"></a>
 
-The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each holds, listed a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is shown as having none rather than left blank `[REQ-VET-001]`.
+The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each holds, listed a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is shown as having none rather than left blank `[REQ-VET-001]`. The same directory is also served in a machine-readable form at a supported endpoint, returning the same veterinarians and their specialties `[REQ-VET-003]`.
+
+Either surface can be narrowed to the veterinarians holding one named specialty. On the directory page the specialty name is supplied as an optional query parameter, and the page then lists only the veterinarians who hold it, still a page at a time, with the parameter carried on the pagination links so the filtered pages stay navigable `[REQ-VET-004]`. The machine-readable endpoint accepts the same optional parameter and returns only the matching veterinarians `[REQ-VET-003]`. Matching is on the whole specialty name and ignores letter case; it is not a prefix match. A name matching no veterinarian yields the normal page or document with an empty veterinarian list. An empty or whitespace-only value behaves as though the parameter were absent — the full directory — mirroring the empty owner search. Without the parameter both surfaces behave as they do today. Neither surface gains a form, dropdown, or other page control in this scope: the filter is a URL contract only.
 
 **Done when:**
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given the clinic's veterinarians, when the directory is opened, then each name and its specialties are listed a page at a time.
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian is shown as having none.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given no specialty parameter, when the machine-readable endpoint is requested, then it returns every veterinarian and their specialties.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty naming a held specialty, when the machine-readable endpoint is requested with it, then it returns only the veterinarians holding that specialty, with a success response.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty matching no veterinarian, when the machine-readable endpoint is requested with it, then it returns a success response carrying an empty veterinarian list.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given an empty or whitespace-only specialty, when the machine-readable endpoint is requested with it, then it returns every veterinarian, as if the parameter were absent.
+- `[REQ-VET-004]` given no specialty parameter, when the directory page is opened, then it lists every veterinarian a page at a time, as today.
+- `[REQ-VET-004]` given a specialty naming a held specialty, when the directory page is opened with it, then only the veterinarians holding that specialty are listed, a page at a time.
+- `[REQ-VET-004]` given a filtered directory spanning more than one page, when a pagination link is followed, then the link carries the specialty and the next page stays filtered.
+- `[REQ-VET-004]` given a specialty matching no veterinarian, when the directory page is opened with it, then the page is shown with an empty veterinarian list and a success response.
+- `[REQ-VET-004]` given an empty or whitespace-only specialty, when the directory page is opened with it, then every veterinarian is listed, as if the parameter were absent.
 
 **Edge cases:**
 1. A veterinarian's specialties are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
-2. **Known defect.** A second route returns the same list in a machine-readable form. Nothing consumes it, and it carries no requirement — see the Superseded list.
+2. Matching is on the whole specialty name, not a prefix: a value that is only part of a specialty name matches no veterinarian, on both surfaces.
+3. The specialty match ignores letter case: a value differing from a held specialty only by letter case matches, on both surfaces.
 
-**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
