+**Specialty filter (both vet surfaces).** The paged `/vets.html` page and the machine-readable `/vets` endpoint each accept an optional `specialty` query parameter. A blank or whitespace-only value is treated as absent and returns the full directory; a non-blank value narrows the result to the veterinarians holding a specialty whose whole name matches case-insensitively — not a prefix. The controller strips the value and branches to the unfiltered `findAll` when blank, mirroring the owner last-name search in `OwnerController`; the non-blank case is a Spring Data derived query on `VetRepository` traversing the vet-to-specialty association. A value matching no specialty yields a normal page or document carrying an empty list and a success response. See [prd.md#req-vet-003](prd.md#req-vet-003), [prd.md#req-vet-004](prd.md#req-vet-004), and the [directory-filter ADR](adr/2026-08-24-non-goal-vet-directory-filter.md).
